\mt1 Malaki
\mt2 (Malachi)
\is1 Introduction
\ip This document records some of God's messages that were given to the prophet Malaki (more accurately ‘Malʼākī’, although traditionally spelt as ‘Malachi’) to pass on to the Israeli people. It was written around 500 years before Yeshua/Jesus (B.C.) once the replacement temple was finished in Yerushalem (Jerusalem). The main purpose of the messages is to encourage the priests and the people to turn back to God and obey him from their hearts. It's apparent that many of them were no longer obeying and worshipping God. The priests and the people were short-changing God by offering second-class animals for the sacrifices and none of them were following God's desires. But God intervened in order to judge and restore his people, and he will send a teacher to precede him to prepare the path and to restore his agreement.
\iot Main components of this account
\io1 The sins of the Israelis \ior 1:1–2:16\ior*
\io1 God's judgement and mercy \ior 2:17–4:6\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
\c 1
\p
\v 1 This is a message¦380162 that Yahweh¦380164 gave to¦380165 Malaki¦380169 for the Israelis¦380167:
\s1 Yahweh's love for the Israelis
\rem /s1 The Lord's Love for Israel; Jacob Loved, Esau Hated; Religious decline and hope of recovery; Israel Preferred to Edom; The Lord's Love for Israel
\p
\v 2 “I¦380171 have¦380171 loved¦380171 you¦380172 all,” says¦380173 Yahweh¦380174, \add ≈but¦380175\add* you¦380175 say¦380175, “How¦380176 have¦380177 you¦380177 \add shown your\add* love¦380177 for us¦380177?”
\p “Wasn't Esaw¦380181 Yacob's¦380182 brother¦380180?” \add ≈declares¦380183\add* Yahweh¦380185. “Yet I've¦380186 loved¦380186 Yacob¦380189\x + \xo 1:2-3: \xt Rom 9:13.\x*
\v 3 and¦380191 \add ≈rejected\add* Esaw¦380193. I've¦380195 turned the hills¦380198 \add where Esaw lived\add* into a¦380199 wasteland¦380199 and¦380200 \add given\add* his¦380202 inheritance¦380202 to the wild jackals¦380203.”
\p
\v 4 If¦380206 \add Esaw's descendants in\add* Edom¦380209 say¦380208, “We've¦380210 \add ≈been¦380210 crushed¦380210\add*, but¦380211 we'll¦380211 return¦380211 and¦380212 \add ≈rebuild¦380212 what was destroyed¦380213\add*,” then army-commander Yahweh¦380216 will say¦380215, “They might build¦380219, but¦380220 I will¦380221 tear¦380221 down¦380221. Others will¦380222 call¦380222 them¦380223 ‘The country¦380224 of¦380224 wickedness¦380225’ and¦380226 ‘The¦380226 people¦380226 who Yahweh¦380230 is forever¦380233 angry¦380229 with.’
\p
\v 5 Your¦380235 own¦380235 eyes¦380235 will¦380236 see¦380236 it, and¦380237 you'll¦380238 say¦380238, ‘Yahweh¦380240 is¦380239 great¦380239 even outside Yisrael's¦380243 \add #borders¦380242\add*.’ ”
\s1 Second-class sacrifices
\rem /s1 The Lord Reprimands the Priests; Unworthy Sacrifices; Blemished Sacrifices; Corruption of the Priesthood
\p
\v 6 “A¦380245 son¦380245 honours¦380246 his father¦380247, and¦380248 a¦380248 servant¦380248 \add ≡honours¦380246\add* his¦380249 master, \add ≈so¦380250\add* if¦380250 I'm a¦380252 father¦380252, where¦380254 is¦380255 my¦380255 honour¦380255? If¦380256 I am¦380258 a¦380258 master¦380258, where¦380260 is¦380261 my¦380261 respect?” says¦380262 army-commander Yahweh¦380264 to¦380266 all you¦380266 priests¦380267 who¦380268 despise¦380268 my name.
\p “But¦380270 you¦380270 say¦380270, ‘How¦380271 have¦380272 we¦380272 despised¦380272 your¦380275 name?’
\v 7 By offering polluted food¦380281 on¦380278 my¦380280 altar¦380280. But¦380283 you¦380283 say¦380283, ‘How¦380284 have¦380285 we¦380285 polluted you¦380285?’ By¦380286 saying¦380286 that Yahweh's¦380288 table¦380287 can \add just\add* be¦380289 disrespected.
\v 8 Don't you think it's wrong when¦380292 you¦380294 sacrifice¦380296 blind¦380295 animals? Isn't¦380297 it evil¦380298 when¦380299 you¦380300 offer lame¦380301 or sick¦380302 \add ≡animals\add*? Try presenting them to¦380307 your¦380307 governor¦380307! Will¦380308 he¦380308 welcome you¦380308 or¦380312 would¦380313 he¦380313 \add ≈be¦380308 offended\add*?” says¦380315 army-commander Yahweh¦380316.\x + \xo 1:8: \xt Deu 15:21.\x*
\p
\v 9 \add ≈So¦380319 now¦380319\add* bring you requests to God¦380325 and \add ≈hope to be¦380329 showered by his grace\add*. \add Ha,\add* army-commander Yahweh¦380335 \add ≈asks¦380334 how he¦380334 could treat you all favourably¦380326 when you're¦380332 bringing second-class offerings\add*?
\p
\v 10 “Yeah, if only there¦380349 was¦380341 one \add >person\add* among¦380341 you¦380341 who¦380338 would¦380342 shut¦380342 the¦380343 \add temple\add* gates so¦380344 that you¦380346 all couldn't \add just continue\add* to light¦380346 worthless fires on my¦380347 altar¦380347. I get no pleasure¦380352 from you¦380353 all,” says¦380354 army-commander Yahweh¦380355, “and¦380357 I¦380360 won't accept¦380360 any offering¦380357 \add ≈that you all bring me\add*.
\v 11 People in other countries from¦380364 the¦380364 east \add all the way\add* to the¦380366 west will honour me, and incense¦380376 and¦380379 genuine sacrifices will be offered¦380379 to me, because¦380381 my¦380384 \add ≈reputation\add* in those countries¦380385 will be praised,” says¦380386 army-commander Yahweh¦380387.
\v 12 “But¦380390 you¦380390 all are¦380391 dishonouring \add @my¦380392 name¦380392\add* when you say¦380393 that the¦380394 master's¦380395 table¦380394 is¦380396 polluted, and¦380398 that its fruit¦380398, its¦380398 food¦380400, can be treated with contempt.
\v 13 You¦380402 all also say¦380402, ‘How tiresome this is,’ and¦380405 you¦380405 snort at¦380405 it¦380406,” says army-commander Yahweh¦380408. “You¦380410 all bring¦380410 \add animals\add* for \add &your\add* offering¦380421 that were killed by a wild animal or is lame¦380414 or sick¦380417. Should I¦380422 accept¦380422 those from¦380424 you?” says Yahweh¦380426.
\v 14 “May the cheats be¦380429 cursed¦380429 who¦380430 have male¦380433 animals in their \add #flocks¦380432\add* and¦380434 vow¦380434 to give them, but¦380435 instead sacrifices¦380435 a¦380436 second-class animal to¦380437 the¦380437 master¦380437! Yes, I'm a¦380439 powerful¦380440 king¦380439,” says¦380442 army-commander Yahweh¦380443, “and¦380445 my¦380445 name¦380445 will be¦380446 carefully respected¦380446 among¦380447 the nations¦380447.”
\c 2
\s1 A warning for the priests
\rem /s1 Admonition for the Priests; A Warning for the Priests
\p
\v 1 Now¦380449 you¦380450 priests¦380453, this¦380452 command¦380451 is for all of you:
\v 2 Army-commander Yahweh¦380470 says¦380469, “If¦380455 you¦380458 all won't listen¦380458 and¦380459 won't¦380461 \add ≈decide in your minds¦380465\add* to¦380466 honour¦380467 to¦380468 my¦380468 \add ≈reputation¦380468\add*, then¦380472 I'll¦380472 send¦380472 a curse on¦380473 you¦380473 all—\add ≈in fact\add* I'll¦380477 curse¦380477 your¦380480 blessings¦380480. Indeed, I've¦380482 \add already\add* cursed¦380482 them, because¦380483 you¦380484 all are¦380485 not \add ≈internalising\add* \add <my instructions\add*.
\v 3 Listen, I'm¦380490 about¦380491 to¦380491 rebuke¦380491 \add &your¦380495\add* descendants¦380495, and¦380496 I'll¦380496 spread¦380496 the¦380501 offal from your¦380502 \add #festivals¦380502\add* on your¦380502 faces¦380500, and¦380503 you all will¦380503 be taken¦380503 away¦380503 with it¦380505.
\v 4 That's so¦380507 you'll¦380507 all know¦380507 that¦380508 it's me who sent¦380509 this¦380513 command¦380512 to¦380510 you¦380510: so that¦380513 my¦380515 agreement¦380515 with¦380516 the Levites can continue,” says¦380519 army-commander Yahweh¦380520.\x + \xo 2:4: \xt Num 3:11-13.\x*
\p
\v 5 “My¦380523 agreement with¦380526 \add @your¦380526 ancestor¦380526 Levi¦380526\add* was \add to give\add* life¦380527 and¦380528 peace¦380528, and¦380529 I¦380529 gave¦380529 them¦380529 to¦380531 \add #them\add*. It¦380531 was an agreement \add ≈based on respect¦380532\add*, and¦380533 \add #they\add* respected¦380533 me¦380533 and¦380534 \add ≈honoured\add* my¦380535 name¦380535.\x + \xo 2:5: \xt Num 25:12.\x*
\v 6 \add ≈They taught the people what was¦380541 right and¦380543 true—they didn't¦380544 tell lies\add*. \add #They\add* \add ≈worked for me peacefully¦380548 and¦380549 loyally\add*, and¦380552 they \add ≈encouraged many¦380552 people to stop disobeying\add*.
\v 7 \add ≈Yes,\add* \add #priests¦380559\add* should pass on knowledge¦380562 and¦380563 people¦380564 should look¦380564 to \add #them\add* \add ≈for good teaching¦380563\add*, because¦380566 they are¦380567 army-commander Yahweh's¦380568 messengers¦380570.
\p
\v 8 But¦380573 you all have¦380574 turned¦380574 away from¦380575 \add that\add* path¦380577 and have¦380578 caused¦380578 many¦380579 \add >people\add* to¦380578 stumble¦380578 \add ≈because of what you've taught\add*—you¦380581 all have¦380581 corrupted¦380581 the¦380582 agreement¦380582 with Levi¦380583,” says¦380584 army-commander Yahweh¦380585.
\v 9 “\add ≈So¦380588\add* that's¦380599 why I've¦380591 caused¦380591 you¦380592 all to be despised¦380593 by all¦380595 the¦380597 people¦380597 and humiliated—because you¦380600 all haven't \add ≈followed me\add*, but¦380605 rather you've¦380605 been¦380605 biased in¦380607 matters of the law.”
\s1 The people have been unfaithful
\rem /s1 A Call to Faithfulness; The Covenant Profaned by Judah; Judah Unfaithful; The People's Unfaithfulness to God
\p
\v 10 Don't¦380610 we all have one father¦380611? Didn't the one¦380612 God¦380615 create¦380617 us¦380617 all? \add So\add* why¦380618 do¦380619 we¦380619 cheat each¦380620 other, thus disrespecting the¦380623 agreement¦380623 with our¦380624 ancestors¦380624?
\v 11 \add Our nation of\add* Yehudah¦380627 \add !(Judah¦380627)\add* has been¦380629 unfaithful \add to Yahweh\add* and done¦380629 \add ≈detestable¦380628\add* things in¦380630 Yisrael¦380630 and¦380631 in¦380631 Yerushalem¦380631. \add ≈Our men\add* have¦380634 defiled¦380634 the¦380636 temple that¦380638 Yahweh¦380637 loves¦380639 by \add ≈marrying¦380640 foreign¦380644 women who worship pagan gods¦380643\add*.
\v 12 May Yahweh¦380647, the one who¦380649 is awake and¦380652 the one¦380652 who¦380652 answers¦380652, banish the \add #men¦380648\add* who do¦380650 this from¦380653 Yisrael, even if \add #they\add* are bringing¦380655 an¦380656 offering¦380656 to¦380657 army-commander Yahweh¦380657.
\p
\v 13 Secondly¦380662, you¦380663 cover¦380664 Yahweh's¦380669 altar¦380668 with tears¦380665 from all your weeping¦380670 and¦380671 groaning¦380671 because he still¦380673 ignores \add &your¦380677\add* \add #offerings¦380677\add* and¦380678 won't¦380672 accept what you all bring¦380678 to him.
\v 14 \add ≈So¦380682\add* you¦380682 \add ≈ask¦380682\add*, “Why not?” \add Well,\add* it's because¦380687 Yahweh¦380689 can testify¦380690 that you've¦380691 been unfaithful to the¦380694 wife¦380694 that you¦380697 \add ≈married\add* when you¦380698 were young¦380695, even though she¦380700 was¦380701 your¦380701 companion¦380701, and¦380702 despite your¦380703 vows.
\v 15 Didn't¦380705 \add @Yahweh¦380708\add* make¦380708 \add you and your wife\add* one and¦380709 give you some of¦380709 his spirit¦380710 because he wanted¦380714 godly children¦380715 \add to come from your marriage\add*? \add ≈So¦380717\add* guard¦380717 yourselves in¦380718 your spirit, and¦380719 don't be unfaithful to the¦380719 \add ≈woman¦380719 you married when you were young¦380720\add*.
\p
\v 16 “Indeed, \add %I¦380727\add* hate¦380727 divorce,” says Yahweh¦380730, the¦380731 god¦380731 of¦380731 Yisrael¦380732, “and¦380733 \add ≈so-called ‘good people’ who are actually cruel\add*,” says army-commander Yahweh¦380739. “So¦380741 \add ≈listen¦380741 to your¦380742 consciences\add* and¦380743 don't¦380743 be unfaithful.”
\s1 Judgement day is coming
\rem /s1 The Day of Judgment; The Day of Judgment Is Near
\p
\v 17 You've¦380747 all wearied¦380747 Yahweh¦380748 with¦380749 your¦380749 words¦380749, and¦380750 \add yet\add* you¦380750 \add ≈ask¦380750\add*, “How¦380751 have we¦380752 wearied¦380752 him¦380752?” By¦380753 saying¦380753, “Yahweh \add ≈is pleased\add* \add even\add* with \add #those\add* who¦380756 do¦380756 evil¦380757, and he's happy with \add all\add* of them¦380762,” or¦380765 “Where¦380766 is¦380767 the¦380767 god¦380767 of¦380767 justice¦380768?”
\c 3
\rem /s1 The Coming Day of Judgment; The Coming Messenger
\p
\v 1 “Listen, I'm¦380770 about¦380771 to¦380771 send¦380771 my¦380772 messenger and¦380773 he'll¦380773 prepare¦380773 the path¦380775 ahead¦380776 of me¦380776. Then¦380777 the¦380782 master¦380782 who¦380784 you're¦380786 all \add ≈looking¦380787 for¦380787\add* will suddenly¦380777 come¦380778 to¦380779 his¦380781 temple¦380781, \add yes,\add* the¦380788 messenger¦380788 who¦380790 you¦380792 are¦380793 all happy about¦380796—the party to¦380796 the agreement¦380789—he'll¦380778 come¦380796,” says¦380797 army-commander Yahweh¦380798.\x + \xo 3:1: \xt Mat 11:10; Mrk 1:2; Luk 1:76; 7:27.\x*
\v 2 \add ≈But¦380801 who¦380801 could survive¦380802 it when he comes¦380806\add*? Who can stand¦380808 when¦380809 he appears¦380809, because¦380810 he'll¦380812 be¦380813 like¦380813 the¦380813 refiner's¦380814 fire¦380813 and¦380815 like¦380815 the¦380815 cleaners' \add powerful\add* soap¦380815?\x + \xo 3:2: \xt Yoel 2:11; Rev 6:17.\x*
\v 3 \add @Yahweh¦380818\add* will¦380818 act as a refiner and¦380820 purifier¦380820 of silver¦380821, and¦380822 he¦380822 will¦380822 purify¦380822 Levi's¦380827 descendants¦380825 \add the priests\add*—\add yes,\add* he'll¦380828 refine¦380828 \add &you all\add* \add with fire\add* like¦380830 gold¦380830 and¦380831 silver¦380831, and¦380832 \add &you'll\add* bring¦380834 \add #offerings¦380835\add* to¦380833 \add *him¦380833\add* that are \add ≈acceptable\add*.
\v 4 \add After that,\add* the¦380840 \add #offerings¦380840\add* of¦380840 \add the people of\add* Yehudah¦380841 and¦380842 Yerushalem¦380842 will be pleasing¦380838 to¦380839 Yahweh¦380839, as¦380843 in \add ≈ancient¦380844 times\add*, and¦380845 as¦380845 in previous¦380846 years¦380845.
\p
\v 5 This is what army-commander Yahweh¦380871 says¦380870, “At that time, I'll¦380848 come¦380848 to¦380849 you¦380849 all to \add ≈judge¦380850\add* you. I'll¦380851 quickly¦380854 testify against all those who¦380854 practice sorcery¦380855, \add ≡against\add* adulterers¦380856, \add ≡against\add* those who \add ≈lie in court\add*, \add ≡against\add* those who \add ≈don't pay their workers fairly\add*, \add ≡against\add* those who mistreat \add #widows¦380863\add* and¦380864 orphans¦380864, \add ≡against\add* those¦380865 who¦380865 \add ≈don't treat the foreigners¦380867 among you decently\add*, and¦380868 \add ≡against\add* those who \add ^refuse to honour\add* me¦380869.
\s1 Giving a tenth
\rem /s1 The Payment of Tithes; Robbing God; A Call to Repentance
\p
\v 6 “I¦380875 am Yahweh¦380876 and I¦380878 don't change¦380878—that's the¦380880 \add only\add* reason why you descendants¦380880 of¦380880 Yacob¦380882 haven't been destroyed.
\v 7 Ever since the¦380886 time¦380886 when your¦380887 ancestors¦380887 were alive, you¦380888 all have¦380888 \add ≈ignored my¦380889 commands\add* and¦380890 \add ^refused to obey\add* them¦380891. \add Now\add* return¦380892 to¦380893 me¦380893—\add if you all do so,\add* I'll¦380894 return¦380894 to¦380895 you¦380895. That's what I, army-commander Yahweh¦380897, say¦380896. But¦380899 you¦380899 all ask¦380899, ‘How¦380900 can we¦380901 return¦380901 to you?’
\rem /s1 Don't rob God
\v 8 Can a human rob¦380903 God¦380905? \add Yes,\add* you're¦380907 all robbing¦380908 me¦380909, but¦380910 you¦380910 ask¦380910, ‘How¦380911 are we¦380912 robbing¦380912 you¦380912?’ \add By failing to give\add* a tenth plus¦380914 offerings¦380914.
\v 9 You're¦380917 all¦380923 cursed¦380918 because you're¦380920 robbing¦380921 me—the¦380922 whole nation¦380922 of¦380923 you.
\v 10 Bring¦380925 the¦380930 full tenth into¦380931 the¦380933 temple¦380933 storeroom¦380934, so¦380935 that there'll be food¦380936 in¦380937 my¦380937 house \add for the temple workers\add*,” says¦380941 army-commander Yahweh¦380942. “\add In fact,\add* you all can test¦380938 me¦380938 \add ≈by¦380940 doing that¦380940 and see\add* if¦380944 I¦380947 don't open¦380947 the¦380950 windows¦380950 of¦380950 \add #heaven¦380951\add* for you all and¦380952 pour¦380952 out¦380952 an \add ≈overflowing\add* blessing¦380954 for¦380953 you¦380953.\x + \xo 3:10: \xt Lev 27:30; Num 18:21-24; Deu 12:6; 14:22-29; Neh 13:12.\x*
\v 11 I'll¦380961 rebuke¦380961 the devourer\f + \fr 3:11 \ft This is literally the ‘eater’ which could refer to some kind of insect (and hence ‘\+em it\+em* won't destroy’ in the next clause) or it could refer to some spiritual power (then you'd get ‘\+em he\+em* won't destroy’).\f* for¦380962 you¦380962 all, so¦380964 that it¦380966 won't destroy¦380966 your crops, and the¦380970 fruit¦380970 off your \add #vines¦380976\add* in¦380977 the¦380977 countryside¦380977 won't be lost,” says¦380978 army-commander Yahweh¦380979.
\v 12 “Then¦380982 all¦380984 the¦380986 other countries¦380986 would say that you've all been blessed¦380982, because¦380987 your land¦380991 \add ≈would¦380989 be¦380989 prosperous\add*,” says¦380993 army-commander Yahweh¦380994.
\s1 God promises mercy for some
\rem /s1 The righteous triumphant; God's Promise of Mercy
\p
\v 13 “Your¦381000 words¦381000 against me have¦380998 been¦380998 harsh,” says¦381001 Yahweh¦381002. “But¦381003 you¦381003 all say¦381003, ‘What¦381004 have¦381006 we¦381006 said¦381006 among ourselves against you¦381007?’
\v 14 You've¦381009 all said¦381009, ‘It's \add ≈a waste of time\add* serving¦381011 God¦381012. What¦381013 did we¦381017 gain¦381015 by keeping¦381017 his¦381018 requirements¦381018, or by \add ≈being sorrowful\add* in¦381022 front¦381022 of¦381022 army-commander Yahweh¦381023?
\v 15 \add ≈It seems that arrogant¦381029 people are¦381032 happier\add*. Evil¦381034 people not only prosper, but they¦381036 \add even\add* \add ≈challenge God¦381037 yet nothing happens to them\add*.’ ”
\rem /s1 The Reward of the Faithful; The Lord's Promise of Mercy
\p
\v 16 Then¦381040 those¦381042 who \add ≈still respected¦381042\add* Yahweh¦381043 spoke¦381041 with¦381045 one another. Yahweh¦381049 paid¦381048 attention¦381048 and¦381050 listened¦381050, and \add ≈while he watched\add*, a¦381052 book of¦381052 remembrance¦381053 was¦381051 written¦381051 about¦381055 those¦381055 who respected¦381055 Yahweh¦381056 and honoured his¦381058 name¦381058.
\v 17 “They'll¦381060 be¦381060 mine,” says¦381062 army-commander Yahweh¦381063. “On the day¦381065 when¦381066 I¦381067 \add ≈assemble\add* my treasured possession¦381069, I¦381070 \add ^won't punish\add* \add @those¦381071 people¦381071\add*, just¦381072 like¦381072 a \add ≈father\add* \add ^doesn't punish\add* his¦381077 son¦381077 who¦381078 \add ≈obeys\add* him¦381079.
\v 18 Then once again you'll all \add ≈be able to see¦381082 the difference\add* between¦381083 righteous¦381084 \add >people\add* and¦381085 wicked¦381085 \add >people\add*—between¦381086 \add #those\add* who¦381087 serve¦381087 God¦381088 and¦381089 \add #those\add* who¦381089 don't¦381090.
\c 4
\s1 Be ready for future judgement
\rem /s1 The Day of the Lord; The Coming Day of Judgment; The Day of the Lord Is Coming; The Great Day of the Lord
\p
\v 1 “\add ≈Yes,\add* listen, the¦381098 day¦381098 that burns¦381100 like¦381101 a furnace¦381101 is coming, when¦381102 all¦381103 the arrogant¦381105 \add >people\add* and¦381106 all¦381106 the evildoers will become \add ≈useless pieces of dry stalks¦381110 in a field\add*. The¦381113 day¦381113 that¦381114 is¦381114 coming¦381114 will burn them up,” says¦381115 army-commander Yahweh¦381116, “so \add ≈they'll¦381102 be¦381102 gone without leaving¦381121 any\add* \add #roots¦381123\add* or \add #branches¦381124\add*.
\v 2 But for¦381128 you¦381128 who respect¦381129 my¦381130 name¦381130, the sun¦381131 of¦381131 righteousness¦381132 will rise¦381127 \add ≈and¦381133 bring\add* healing¦381133. You'll¦381135 all go¦381135 out¦381135, jumping around¦381136 like¦381137 calves¦381137 \add let out of\add* \add &their¦381138\add* stall¦381138,
\v 3 and¦381141 you'll¦381141 all trample¦381141 down¦381141 the wicked¦381142 \add >people\add*, because¦381143 they'll¦381145 \add just\add* be¦381145 ashes¦381146 under¦381147 the¦381148 soles¦381148 of¦381148 your¦381149 feet¦381149 on the¦381150 day¦381150 that I¦381152 act¦381153,” says¦381154 army-commander Yahweh¦381155.
\p
\v 4 “\add ≈Be sure to obey\add* the¦381161 law that¦381164 I¦381165 \add ≈gave\add* my¦381163 servant¦381163 Mosheh¦381162 at¦381167 \add ≈Mt. Sinai\add* for all¦381170 Israel¦381172—the statutes¦381173 and¦381174 the rulings.
\p
\v 5 Listen, I'll¦381178 send¦381179 the¦381183 prophet¦381183 Eliyah¦381182 to¦381184 you all, \add ahead\add* of the¦381184 coming¦381185 of¦381184 the¦381186 great¦381188 \add ≈but\add* fearful day¦381186 of¦381186 \add *my¦381187\add* \add judgement\add*.\x + \xo 4:5: \xt Mat 11:14; 17:10-13; Mrk 9:11-13; Luk 1:17; Yhn 1:21.\x*
\v 6 He'll¦381192 \add ≈restore harmony between fathers¦381195 and¦381199 their¦381203 children\add*, so that I¦381206 don't \add have to\add* come¦381206 and¦381207 strike¦381207 the¦381210 earth¦381210 with complete¦381211 destruction¦381211.”
